{"title":"JEE Advanced","category":"Engineering","bank":"jee_advanced","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Basics of Mathematics","count":6,"questions":[{"id":25286,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Basics of Mathematics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Let $a=3 \\sqrt{2}$ and $b=\\frac{1}{5^{1 / 6} \\sqrt{6}}$. If $x, y \\in \\mathbb{R}$ are such that\n$\\begin{gathered}3 x+2 y=\\log _a(18)^{\\frac{5}{4}} \\\\2 x-y=\\log _b(\\sqrt{1080})\\end{gathered}$\nand then $4 x+5 y$ is equal to . ________.","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"$\\begin{aligned} & 3 x+2 y=\\log _{3 \\sqrt{2}}(3 \\sqrt{2})^{\\frac{5}{2}}=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\quad 6 x+4 y=5 \\quad \\ldots \\ldots(1)\\end{aligned}2 x-y=\\log _{\\frac{1}{5^{1 / 6} \\sqrt{6}}}\\left(5^{\\frac{1}{6}} \\sqrt{6}\\right)^3=-3\\begin{array}{ll}\\Rightarrow & 2 x-y=-3 \\quad.....(2)\\\\ & \\text { equation (1) }-(2) \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\quad & 4 x+5 y=8\\end{array}$","difficulty":"Easy","source":"JEE Advanced 2024 (Paper 1)","_marksId":"66965dcdd603121f43a3e5d1","questionType":"numerical","_advSection":"NUM","type":"numerical","correctValue":8},{"id":25287,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Basics of Mathematics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"The product of all positive real values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> satisfying the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>68</mn><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup></math> is","options":[],"answer":"1","solution":"<blockquote><p>Taking log to the base <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> on both sides</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>68</mn><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>68</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Hence, the product is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p></blockquote>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"JEE Advanced 2022 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"64b16a9ef23ac7d519f9b611","_advSection":"NUM","questionType":"numerical","type":"numerical","correctValue":"1"},{"id":25288,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Basics of Mathematics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"The value of <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math> is_____.","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow>