</math><br  /><math><mo>=</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>","difficulty":"Easy","source":"JEE Advanced 2018 (Paper 1)","_marksId":"64b16a68f23ac7d519f9b428","questionType":"numerical","correctValue":"8","_advSection":"NUM","type":"numerical"},{"id":25289,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Basics of Mathematics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"<p>If <math> <mrow> <msup> <mn>3</mn> <mtext>x</mtext> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mn>4</mn> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math>, then x =</p>","options":["<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>2 log</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>2 log</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mn>2</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>","<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mo>-</mo> <msub> <mtext>log</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>","<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>-</mo> <msub> <mtext>log</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>","<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>2 log</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>2 log</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mn>3</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"3<sup>x</sup> = 4<sup>x</sup><sup> - 1</sup><br  />x = (x - 1) log<sub>3</sub> 4<br  />x ( 1 - 2 log<sub>3</sub> 2) = -2log<sub>3</sub> 2<br  /><math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>log</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>log</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mn>2</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br  />x log<sub>2</sub> 3 = (x - 1).2<br  />x (log<sub>2</sub> 3 - 2) = -2<br  /><math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>log</mtext> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br  /><math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <msub> <mtext>log</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>-</mo> <msub> <mtext>log</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"JEE Advanced 2013 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"64b16a30f23ac7d519f9b223","_advSection":"MC","questionType":"multipleCorrect","type":"multipleCorrect","answers":[0,1,2]},{"id":25290,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Basics of Mathematics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Let $\\left(x_0, y_0\\right)$ be the solution of the following equations $(2 x)^{\\log 2}=(3 y)^{\\log 3}$, $3^{\\log x}=2^{\\log y}$, then $x_0$ is equal to","options":["$\\frac{1}{6}$","$\\frac{1}{2}$","$\\frac{1}{2}$","6"],"answer":2,"solution":"Taking log on both sides,\n\n\\log 2 \\cdot \\log (2 x)=\\log 3(\\log 3 y)\n\n\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\Rightarrow & \\log 2\\{\\log 2+\\log x\\} \\\\\n& =\\log 3\\{\\log 3+\\log y\\} \\\\\n\\text { and } & \\log x \\cdot \\log 3=\\log y \\log 2 \\\\\n& \\log y=\\frac{\\log x \\cdot \\log 3}{\\log 2}\n\\end{array}\n\nFrom Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get\n\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\log 2\\{\\log 2+\\log x\\} \\\\\n&=\\log 3 \\cdot\\left\\{\\log 3+\\frac{\\log x \\cdot \\log 3}{\\log 2}\\right\\} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad(\\log 2)^2+\\log 2 \\cdot \\log x \\\\\n&=(\\log 3)^2+\\frac{(\\log 3)^2}{(\\log 2)} \\cdot \\log x \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\log x\\left\\{\\frac{(\\log 3)^2}{\\log 2}-\\log 2\\right\\} \\\\\n&=(\\log 2)^2-(\\log 3)^2\n\\end{aligned}\n\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\log x=-\\log 2=\\log 2^{-1} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad x=\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n","difficulty":"Medium","source":"JEE Advanced 2011 (Paper 1)","_marksId":"64b16a0ff23ac7d519f9b0f7","_advSection":"SC","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect"},{"id":25291,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Basics of Mathematics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"JEE Advanced","q":"Match the Statements/Expressions in Column I with the Statements/Expressions in Column II.\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_advanced%252FNV6MxxlCrdeWHLs9r4Y0EOApcJx3jyAt7MA2okb20P0.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_advanced%2FNV6MxxlCrdeWHLs9r4Y0EOApcJx3jyAt7MA2okb20P0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_advanced%2FNV6MxxlCrdeWHLs9r4Y0EOApcJx3jyAt7MA2okb20P0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>","options":["(A) r, (B) q,r, (C) s, (D) p,r","(A) s, (B) q,s, (C) r, (D) p,q","(A) s, (B) q,r, (C) s, (D) p,q","(A) r, (B) q,s, (C) r, (D) p,r"],"answer":3,"solution":"(A) Let $y=\\frac{x^2+2 x+4}{x+2}$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow x^2+(2-y) x+(4-2 y)=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad(2-y)^2-4(4-2 y) \\geq 0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad y^2+4 y-12 \\geq 0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad y \\leq-6, y \\geq 2 \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n\n$\\therefore$ Minimum value of $y$ is 2 .\n(B) Since, $(A+B)(A-B)=(A-B)(A+B)$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad A^2-A B+B A-B^2=A^2+A B-B A-B^2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad A B=B A \\\\\n& \\text { and } \\quad(A B)^t=(-1)^k A B \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad B^t A^t=(-1)^k A B \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad-B A=(-1)^k A B \\quad\\left[\\because B^t=-B, A^t=A\\right] \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad B A=(-1)^{k+1} A B \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad(-1)^{k+1}=1 \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n\n$\\therefore k+1$ is even or $k$ is odd.\n(C) $1 \\lt  2^{\\left(-k+3^{-a}\\right)} \\lt  2 \\Rightarrow 0 \\lt  -k+3^{-a} \\lt  1$\nGiven, $a=\\log _3 \\log _3 2 \\Rightarrow 3^a=\\log _3 2$\n\\begin{array}{lc}\n\\Rightarrow & 3^{-a}=\\log _2 3 \\\\\n\\therefore & k < \\log _2 3 < 2 \\\\\n\\text { and } & 1+k>\\log _2 3>1 \\Rightarrow k>0\n\\end{array}\n\nFrom Eqs. (ii) and (iii), $0 \\lt  k \\lt  2 \\Rightarrow k=1[\\because k$ is an integer]\n\n\\begin{array}{rlrl}\n\\text { (D) } & \\sin \\theta & =\\cos \\phi \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\cos \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right) & =\\cos \\phi \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta & =2 n \\pi \\pm \\phi, n \\in Z \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & & \\theta \\pm \\phi-\\frac{\\pi}{2} & =-2 n \\pi, n \\in Z \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & & \\frac{1}{\\pi}\\left(\\theta \\pm \\phi-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) & =-2 n, n \\in Z\n\\end{array}\n","difficulty":"Hard","source":"JEE Advanced 2008 (Paper 2)","_marksId":"64b169edf23ac7d519f9afc1","_advSection":"SC","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect"}]}